    {
      "id": "tokugawa-ieyasu-yamaoka-s087-p10174",
      "source_en": "There was no longer any sign of the enemy on the riverbank. The order to withdraw had already reached the front lines, and the mournful blare of conch horns sounded from up ahead. It was already the Hour of the Goat. Seventeen hundred of the enemy lay dead. As Nobunaga reckoned the number in his mind, he raised a hand against the sunlight reflected from the surface of the Ane River and gazed toward the narrow road on the opposite bank along which the defeated enemy had fled.",
